**NOW IT IS AGREED as follows:**

**1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

1.1 Terms defined in the Agreement shall have the same meaning in this Amendment unless otherwise defined herein or the context otherwise requires.

1.2 In this Amendment:
- "Solar PV Array" means the 5.2 MWp (DC) photovoltaic solar array installed at the Original Plant site, comprising 12,800 solar modules, inverters, combiner boxes, and associated balance-of-plant equipment, as more particularly described in Schedule 1 to this Amendment.
- "Solar O&M Services" means the operation and maintenance services described in Clause 3 below.

**2. EFFECTIVE DATE**

2.1 This Amendment shall become effective on **15 March 2021** (the "Effective Date"), notwithstanding the date of execution appearing at the foot of this Amendment.

**3. SCOPE OF SERVICES – ADDITION OF SOLAR O&M**

3.1 With effect from the Effective Date, the definition of "Plant" in Clause 1.1 of the Agreement shall be amended to include the Solar PV Array.

3.2 The Contractor shall provide the following additional services in respect of the Solar PV Array (the "Solar O&M Services"):

(a) Routine inspection and preventive maintenance of solar modules, including visual inspection for cracks, hot spots, delamination, and soiling, on a monthly basis;

(b) Cleaning of solar modules using deionised water and soft brushes, at a frequency of at least once per quarter, or more frequently during the harmattan season (typically November to February) when dust accumulation is expected to be higher;

(c) Inspection and preventive maintenance of inverters, including checking of cooling fans, filter cleaning, torque checks on DC connections, and firmware updates as recommended by the inverter manufacturer;

Amendment No. 1 effective date 2021-03-15 date. Record status: historical.

(d) Monitoring of the SCADA system for the Solar PV Array, including daily review of performance data, alarm handling, and reporting of any underperformance;

(e) Corrective maintenance of all solar PV components, including replacement of faulty modules, inverters, fuses, surge protection devices, and other components as necessary, subject to the exclusions in Clause 4 below;

(f) Vegetation control and site housekeeping within the Solar PV Array area, including grass cutting and removal of debris;

(g) Quarterly infrared (thermographic) inspection of all DC combiner boxes and inverter DC inputs to detect hot spots;

(h) Maintenance of the Solar PV Array's access roads and fencing;

(i) Maintaining a spare parts inventory for the Solar PV Array, with a minimum stock level as set out in Schedule 2 to this Amendment; and

(j) Preparation and submission of monthly performance reports, including energy yield, availability, and any incidents or near-misses.

3.3 The Solar O&M Services shall be provided in accordance with the Performance Standards set out in Schedule 3 to this Amendment, including a guaranteed availability of not less than 98.5% for the Solar PV Array (calculated on a monthly basis, excluding force majeure events and periods of grid curtailment beyond the Contractor's control).

